  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support for restructuring and consolidation of new local supply dynamics and strengthening food security and local economies of the northwest region of the State of Rio Grande do Sul</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Centro de Tecnologias Alternativas Populares (CETAP) will expand upon its previous activities to encourage the development and organization of family farms to be ecologically sound. This will include continuing to promote agroecological farming systems with family farmers and the distribution and marketing of organic products in the northwest region of the state of Rio Grande do Sul, Brazil. CETAP will continue facilitating the connection between urban and rural groups. CETAP will also organize and facilitate a regional meeting with grantee-partner working with agroecology during the Ecovida meeting in 2017. These activities will benefit an additional 1,530 family farmers, and low-income urban groups.</narrative>
  </description>
